    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section id="faq" class="container mx-auto px-6 py-20">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-center mb-12">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-4">
            <div class="collapse collapse-plus bg-base-200">
                <input type="radio" name="faq-accordion" />
                <div class="collapse-title text-xl font-medium">What size parts can you scan?</div>
                <div class="collapse-content">
                    <p>We can handle parts from small components (100mm x 100mm x 100mm) up to approximately half the size of a car. If you're unsure whether your part is too large, send us photos and we'll let you know.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="collapse collapse-plus bg-base-200">
                <input type="radio" name="faq-accordion" />
                <div class="collapse-title text-xl font-medium">What materials work best?</div>
                <div class="collapse-content">
                    <p>Matte, non-reflective surfaces scan best. Shiny metal, transparent, or very dark black parts may require special preparation (like temporary coating spray). We'll advise you after reviewing your photos.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="collapse collapse-plus bg-base-200">
                <input type="radio" name="faq-accordion" />
                <div class="collapse-title text-xl font-medium">What if I can't ship it?</div>
                <div class="collapse-content">
                    <p>We can arrange that you come to our facility (Seacoast, NH), or we can travel to you (travel time max 1hr).</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="collapse collapse-plus bg-base-200">
                <input type="radio" name="faq-accordion" />
                <div class="collapse-title text-xl font-medium">Do you offer CAD conversion or reverse engineering?</div>
                <div class="collapse-content">
                    <p>CAD conversion requires understanding design intent, which varies by application - without knowing that the best we can do is recreate your part in Solidworks and give you a STEP file suitable for manufacturing. Price will depend on part geometry and will be discussed before work starts.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="collapse collapse-plus bg-base-200">
                <input type="radio" name="faq-accordion" />
                <div class="collapse-title text-xl font-medium">What if my part gets damaged in shipping?</div>
                <div class="collapse-content">
                    <p>We handle all parts with care, but shipping carries inherent risks. We strongly recommend you purchase shipping insurance for valuable or irreplaceable items. You are responsible for properly packaging your part and insuring shipments both ways.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="collapse collapse-plus bg-base-200">
                <input type="radio" name="faq-accordion" />
                <div class="collapse-title text-xl font-medium">Are the scan files ready to 3D print?</div>
                <div class="collapse-content">
                    <p>The scan files we provide are high-quality meshes, but they may require some cleanup or modification depending on your intended use. Most 3D printing slicers can import STL files directly, though you may need to repair or optimize the mesh for your specific application.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="collapse collapse-plus bg-base-200">
                <input type="radio" name="faq-accordion" />
                <div class="collapse-title text-xl font-medium">Do you ship internationally?</div>
                <div class="collapse-content">
                    <p>Currently we only accept shipments within the United States. International service may be added in the future.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="collapse collapse-plus bg-base-200">
                <input type="radio" name="faq-accordion" />
                <div class="collapse-title text-xl font-medium">What payment methods do you accept?</div>
                <div class="collapse-content">
                    <p>We accept all major credit cards, Venmo and PayPal.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
